// CotSC Batch 34: English item/NPC names and descriptions in five large components.
// Original English text and all installer quest logic are preserved.

@4000 = ~Boots~

@4001 = ~Boots of Traitor~

@4002 = ~These red-and-black boots are surprisingly light and supple despite their age.~

@4003 = ~These scarlet-and-black boots once belonged to an elven warrior charged with defending Firewine as it was destroyed in a magical battle. When he became convinced the defense was doomed, he betrayed those beside him. Under cover of night, he murdered several of his sleeping comrades, stripped them of their belongings, and tried to flee with his stolen spoils.

He never escaped. The dying curse of the warriors he betrayed bound his soul to Firewine, condemning him to linger among the ruins he had abandoned. The boots survived as a bitter reminder of his treachery and still carry a trace of the stealth he used on the night of the murders.

STATISTICS:

Hide in Shadows: +15 points
Move Silently: +10 points
Weight: 4

Not Usable By:
Characters without the Thief class~

@4004 = ~Manticore's Hide~

@4005 = ~This immense section of russet hide was taken from the ancient manticore imprisoned beneath Firewine. Centuries of exposure to unstable arcane energies have changed the leather without ruining it. The hide is unusually dense, warm to the touch, and seems to resist extremes of heat and cold.

A master armorer might be able to fashion something exceptional from material this rare.

Weight: 12~

@4006 = ~Manticore's Mane~

@4007 = ~Fashioned by Taerom Fuiruim from the magically saturated hide of the ancient manticore beneath Firewine, this armor retains part of the strange energy that sustained the beast for centuries. Heat rolls away from its surface, while unnatural cold seems unable to bite through the dense hide.

STATISTICS:

Fire Resistance: +20%
Cold Resistance: +20%~

